WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.200
<i>C'mon, morning's here--time to be on our way</i>

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.700
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.830
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>No turning back: this trip is nonfiction</i>

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:35.080
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>It's now or never, the real deal: Ready, and... action!</i>

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.540
<i>Harsh winds that make us hesitate,</i>
<i>nights spent crying our eyes out</i>

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.790
<i>They're not necessarily bad things (not bad)</i>

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.500
<i>Just like the power in a spring:</i>
<i>the harder we're pushed</i>

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.040
<i>The higher we can fly</i>

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:05.580
<i>Face the far-off distance</i>
<i>and aim for the horizon: rising sun</i>

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.870
<i>Holding our hands up to that morning sun</i>

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:21.250
<i>Our shared feelings brought us together--</i>
<i>we're not alone anymore</i>

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:27.450
<i>And so we're on this brilliant voyage</i>

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:34.250
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:42.290
In the middle of a fierce battle
between Chin and Gi, they meet again:

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:44.830
Shin and Rin Ko.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:48.080
Which of them will overcome his limits

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:50.750
and have his own way in the end?

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:54.330
Their blistering-hot emotions
are making sparks fly!

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.120
Now get down here!

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:01.250
We settle this with a duel!

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:04.910
I'll even take you on bare-handed!

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:05.790
My lord?

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:09.040
Your banter hasn't changed a bit, I see!

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:12.450
Ah, but that's a good thing...

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.080
All right, let's begin!

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:15.410
Yes, sir!

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:16.790
Take your positions!

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:19.370
Round up the troops!

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:21.250
On the double!

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:23.540
You're no fun...

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:31.670
"The Final Twist"

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.620
So Ren Pa didn't come alone after all...

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.540
Of course he didn't!

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.200
What the hell is going on?

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.750
The greatest duties of the headquarters--

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.830
that is, a commander and his staff--

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:13.370
are producing an overall picture
of the battle at hand

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:16.870
and leading its army to victory.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:23.410
The plans both sides had drawn up
shared some common points.

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:31.660
Mou Gou and Ren Pa, though enemies,
were exceedingly close at heart.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:36.870
The overall plan I'd devised for this battle

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:40.910
uses the main central army as a shield

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:47.330
to bear the brunt of the attacks
from Ren Pa's central army.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:48.660
Then,

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.450
in the meantime, the two lieutenants
Kan Ki and Ou Sen

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:55.200
serve as our main attack team
with their great offensive power,

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.580
moving in from both flanks.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:02.450
They will crush the opposing Gi army
and go for their main camp.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:12.120
The Gi army's main attack force
is Rin Ko's army, in the center.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:13.580
However,

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:17.040
we should send our flanks
after the enemy's lieutenants,

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:21.370
destroy them or hold them back,

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:25.660
then surround Mou Gou's main camp.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:27.330
In other words,

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:32.200
our strategy's built on three fields:
left, right, and center.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.910
The same tactics...

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:38.790
Anyone could come up with that much.

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:41.330
But here's where it gets tricky:

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:44.000
We respond in different ways.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:48.120
I've ordered them to focus on defense.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:53.660
I came out swinging--and I won.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:54.870
It's a given.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:05.750
I lost Gen Pou early on,
but then Kai Shi Bou's army rushed in.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.450
In the free-for-all that followed,

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:10.830
Kan Ki's army, some of Chin's hardest hitters,

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:12.410
went silent.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:16.540
That's all it took for us to dominate.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:21.330
What turned the tide more than anything else

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:23.620
was the right-flank battle.

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:29.500
My own army mobilized, and Ou Sen's
army retreated far and deep.

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:32.410
No--they <i>ran</i> .

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:40.370
Mou Gou, are you sure you haven't
made some gross miscalculation?

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:44.910
You've lost half of the brawn
you'd been counting on,

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:49.790
and you let me rush
your main camp from behind.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:52.910
I've been working on this for so long--

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:56.540
even putting Haku Ki Sai in charge
was all part of my plan.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:59.870
Now Rin Ko just has to destroy the central army.

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:02.160
I attack from behind,

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:06.540
the main camp gets caught
in the middle... and it's over.

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:14.040
Nothing to fret about.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:18.160
To him, I'm always a loser.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:19.410
My lord?

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:22.370
Send all the main camp's troops to the back.

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:24.330
A-All of them?!

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:29.080
But when the enemy gets past
the central army at the front--

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.410
I don't care.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:46.080
Ren Pa, I have always lost to you.
I expected this to happen.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:49.120
And having expected it...

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:52.290
...I can cope with it.

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:53.290
Furthermore,

00:06:55.370 --> 00:07:02.040
I built this fortress solely
for you to attack it. Behold:

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:06.040
my Mou Gou-style anti-Ren Pa
counterstrike formation!

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:12.500
You mean he did all this in secret?

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:17.080
I heard he's big on defense,
which means fewer chinks...

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:18.500
Hey, no, wait a second!

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:21.620
Get a load of that fortress!

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:24.950
I know! It's so inelegant--and inefficient, too!

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:28.660
No...

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:30.870
...it's not bad at all.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:35.870
You did pretty well for someone
so mediocre, Mou Gou!

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:43.750
Of course. I've been planning
and plotting this formation for years,

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:49.870
all to draw your attacks when
the day came for us to do battle.

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:57.250
Hmm. This could be tricky...

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:59.950
There are too many horsemen.
Have half of them dismount.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:00.950
Yes, sir!

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:05.660
The archers are fine as is.
Put the shields in front to take the arrows.

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:06.910
Yes, sir!

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:09.830
All right--here we go, Mou Gou.

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:14.330
I'll take your head by my own hand.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:17.330
The enemy is on the move!

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:20.120
Where's Ren Pa striking from?!

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:21.120
My lord!

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.080
Come on, then, Ren Pa.

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:28.120
Enter this fortress and <i>you're</i> the dead man!

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:33.200
Stay aware of your surroundings!

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:36.540
There are enemy soldiers
wandering the area, just like us.

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:37.540
Yes, sir!

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:42.500
We brought up the rear just fine,

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:47.370
but now we're separated from
Ou Sen's squad--and lost, to boot...

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:52.200
We picked up other squads
along the way, so we're plenty strong.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.500
Better get back to the
front lines on the double...

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:00.040
Heki, sir, is that--

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:09.950
General Mou Gou's main camp?!
Just how lost <i>are</i> we?

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:18.830
No! A-Are they under attack?

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:37.870
Ren Pa has mobilized!

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:40.700
C-Commander!

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:42.330
Ren Pa's coming this way!

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:44.580
Don't panic!

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:48.870
That fool! We've got you now, Ren Pa!

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:50.120
Huh?

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:51.830
If you want to avoid a rain of arrows,

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:54.370
it's standard practice to attack from the sides.

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:59.200
That's why we've hidden archers
in the woods on either side.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:04.410
With arrows from the front <i>and</i> sides,
even Ren Pa won't stand a chance!

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:08.540
That's the legendary general Ren Pa for you!

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.660
His tactics are already outdated!

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:13.540
Fire!

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:22.120
A-Are they in their right minds?!

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:25.160
Why would they fire on their allies?

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:27.410
My lord, what <i>is</i> this?

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:29.660
The bordering woods

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:32.200
were already in enemy hands.

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:46.200
R-Ren Pa just went right on in...

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.000
They're breaching the front ranks!

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:50.040
The right edge is done for!

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:51.290
My lord!

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:56.250
Never fear. The true terror of this fortress

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:58.080
starts right now!

00:10:58.080 --> 00:10:59.580
All right!

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:01.620
They're thin on the ground here!

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:02.580
We can do this!

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:04.790
We'll tear Ren Pa apart!

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:08.290
Huh?

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:09.580
What the--

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:11.330
It's...

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:13.080
...a dead end?!

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:14.370
What's going on up there?

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:15.330
What is it?

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:18.000
No! Stay back!

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:25.290
Now! Fire!

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:32.910
General... it appears some
of our squads are done for.

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:37.450
The broken-path strategy:

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:41.160
cutting off pathways to corner the enemy.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:46.790
Unlike Ou Sen's drum-tight fortress,

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:51.250
Mou Gou's is, at first glance,
messy and full of holes.

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:52.660
However...

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:56.040
start to climb it and you'll
discover dead-end routes

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:59.080
that are invisible when viewed from below.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:04.700
Mou Gou planned it that way:
ideal pits for trapping his prey.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:08.000
He sprinkled the entire
fortress with these traps,

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:10.700
laying them out like a maze.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:13.160
This fortress isn't for defense.

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:18.450
No, it's clearly made for striking
back at the foes who enter.

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:23.620
Damn you, Mou Gou...
So you're serious about attacking me.

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:24.660
Amazing!

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:27.790
Here I thought we'd slowed
them down--but we've killed them!

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:31.700
Leave it to our lord to come up
with something like this!

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:36.870
We built it as we were instructed,
but we had no idea...

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:39.040
Talk about a surprise!

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:43.830
What's surprising is how it
shut down Ren Pa's sneak attack!

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:48.290
Did you anticipate his arrival, my lord?

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:52.580
Ren Pa is a general of many faces.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:56.290
Before battle, he is a resourceful general

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:58.080
who comes up with elaborate plans.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:00.830
When the fighting begins,
he's an intuitive general

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:04.120
with his finger on the very pulse of battle.

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:08.620
Once he decides to defend,
he becomes a protective general,

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:11.660
the steel wall that guarded
Shou Hei for two years.

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:15.790
When it's time to attack, he's a fierce general

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:19.910
who strikes with deadly force--
in regular tactics or clever schemes.

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:24.200
He has even been known to
head up his own vanguard,

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:27.370
that's how intrepid he is.

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:28.750
Intrepid...

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:31.500
...and a show-off like none other.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:35.910
So yes, I saw this coming.

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:39.700
Remarkable, my lord! I tip my hat to you.

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:43.830
It's uncanny just how well you know Ren Pa.

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:50.290
Indeed, merely in losing to him
so many times over as a young man,

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:53.580
I came to learn Ren Pa well...

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:56.330
but that's not all.

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:59.870
It's been about forty years
since I came to the land of Chin.

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:03.450
In all the time, I have not fought Ren Pa,
not even once.

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:08.620
Yet I know all the minutest details
of Ren Pa's every battle.

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:11.790
I spent a great deal of money
to gather that information,

00:14:11.790 --> 00:14:16.540
and even secretly went
to watch some battles myself.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:18.450
That's right:

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:20.450
I have always...

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:24.830
...kept a close eye on Ren Pa...

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:29.970
"Ren Pa"

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:37.910
This is the end of the line for you!

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:40.000
Shin!

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:44.790
Shin's fighting so hard over there--
We gotta win this, too!

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:51.950
Don't let the Hi Shin Unit beat you!

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:53.870
Show 'em what we're made of!

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:58.700
Where are you lookin', ya bastard?!

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:03.040
Now!

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:15.040
The other squads are joining up with ours.

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:17.500
If we get too big, we'll never get
out of one of those dead ends!

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:22.410
Don't fret! Just leave it to me.

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:27.750
A new report!

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:30.330
Yesterday, Ren Pa's army
appeared at the right flank

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:33.500
and pushed Ou Sen's army far back!

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:39.250
The general himself at the right...

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:41.700
This doesn't look good for Mou Gou.

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:45.830
Ren Pa must be creeping up
behind him right about now.

00:15:45.830 --> 00:15:50.080
So Mou Gou will have to go
without his revenge after all.

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:52.040
What do you mean?

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:54.160
Hmm? Oh, er...

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:56.290
It's just that Mou Gou
kept losing to General Ren Pa

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:59.410
back when he was in the land of Se.

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:03.870
It's unclear whether Ren Pa remembers this,

00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:08.950
but for Mou Gou, this is their
first revenge match in decades.

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:12.830
I'm from Se myself, you see.

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:15.620
I found it rather moving, and--

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:18.000
Had I not already mentioned it?

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:19.790
R-Ri Boku, sir?

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:24.580
If only you'd said something sooner.

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:25.660
Huh?

00:16:25.660 --> 00:16:27.450
Ri Boku, sir?

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:31.950
I'm almost certain it's not
the case for General Ren Pa,

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:34.660
but when a mighty commander gets tripped up,

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:38.450
there's always a moment of inattention.

00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:43.540
When I fight, I do my utmost
to throw my foe off his guard.

00:16:45.660 --> 00:16:52.370
If the general remembers Mou Gou,
that itself is to Mou Gou's benefit.

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:54.040
That's because the winner

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:57.830
tends to view his opponent
as being of a certain caliber...

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:02.950
What is it?

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:07.870
No... that's right. There's more.

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:14.450
If Mou Gou does harbor
something deep within for Ren Pa...

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:19.410
then he had a full forty years
to perfect a strategy

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:22.290
against his rival.

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:25.450
It's become clear to me at last:

00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:27.790
If Mou Gou is even the slightest bit better

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:31.080
than Ren Pa's <i>idea</i> of Mou Gou...

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:38.040
This way!

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:44.750
Dammit! We just can't manage
to snare Ren Pa's squad!

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:47.450
Damn his luck!

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:51.450
Over here!

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:53.700
Now he's going down?

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:55.750
Another trap dodged!

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:57.410
I-It can't be...

00:17:57.410 --> 00:17:59.750
Does Ren Pa know where the traps are?!

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:05.910
Impossible! You can't see
their layout from below!

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:07.830
There's no way he could know!

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:12.250
Even if he can't see them,
he can guess where they might be.

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:16.410
One can see the entire fortress
from below before entering.

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:19.660
Given where the fences are
and the layout of the mountain,

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:23.500
it wouldn't be impossible
to pinpoint likely spots.

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:26.700
So he looked at the fortress first--
and knew there were traps?

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:31.830
B-But even if--even if he could
work out where they were,

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:35.750
he'd lose the big picture as soon as he went in.

00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:41.620
Memorizing the right path
through such a complex maze so quickly?

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:43.290
It can't be done!

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:45.540
And yet,

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:47.450
Ren Pa has done it.

00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:54.660
He's dodged another one!
They're already halfway up!

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:59.910
All right--raise the flag!
The general's got us on the right path!

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:01.000
Yes, sir!

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:04.000
Whoa! Look!

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:08.290
So he's come at last...

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:13.450
Ren Pa, I know you well.

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:17.080
The talent that allows you
to etch this maze's path into your brain

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:22.200
and follow it to the letter

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:26.000
comes as no surprise. And so,

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:28.410
I shall use your cleverness

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:31.160
against you.

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:32.450
Move them!

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:46.330
Wh-What?!

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:49.410
There's a new path--leading straight to a trap!

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:56.330
There he goes!

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:57.120
Got him!

00:19:57.120 --> 00:19:58.370
We've got him!

00:19:58.370 --> 00:19:59.200
My lord!

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:00.370
Mou Gou, sir!

00:20:00.370 --> 00:20:03.500
Ren Pa... this fortress's greatest weapon,

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:08.160
the product of forty years
of planning and polish...

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:11.330
the maze you figured out in advance?

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:19.450
It can be reconfigured after the fact.

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:20.750
A dead end?!

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:25.750
Aha...

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:27.250
Fire!

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:32.040
Behind me--

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:35.660
I know something's goin' on at the main camp...

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:39.080
but I can't be thinkin' about that right now.

00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:40.080
Right now...

00:20:42.620 --> 00:20:44.870
if I take my eyes off this guy,

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:47.620
I'm a goner!

00:20:52.450 --> 00:20:54.290
Shin...

00:20:54.290 --> 00:20:56.620
Fight alongside the five-man squad there!

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:58.450
Don't give them an inch!

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:03.370
Cavalry fights cavalry!

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:08.700
Infantry, back down!
Men, put all you've got into this one fight!

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:13.620
Shin...

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:17.370
I'll handle the squad. And in return...

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:21.500
...you've got to take Rin Ko's head!

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:28.500
Sorry, En, So Sui...

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:31.750
He's done a fine job stopping my advance.

00:21:31.750 --> 00:21:34.870
Partly thanks to that
wheel thinning the ranks...

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:38.790
but these intervening
Hi Shin troops are powerful, too:

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:40.250
both the cavalry

00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:42.080
and the infantry.

00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:47.330
Then there's the other squads
who answered the call to join the fray.

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:52.870
In short, the source of the Chin army's
morale around here

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:57.040
is the leader of the Hi Shin Unit: Shin.

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:02.580
This young man here.
He's practically playing general already.

00:22:03.910 --> 00:22:06.290
His military might aside,

00:22:06.290 --> 00:22:11.290
I didn't have his magnetism,
his charisma at that age.

00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:15.080
This young man really is...

00:22:17.830 --> 00:22:21.500
Do you understand the
significance of this undertaking,

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:23.830
Shin of the Hi Shin Unit?

00:22:23.830 --> 00:22:27.870
If you fall, the Chin army
here will be destroyed,

00:22:27.870 --> 00:22:31.250
and we'll rush off to kill Mou Gou.

00:22:31.250 --> 00:22:35.500
Keep on babblin'! If I take <i>you</i> down,

00:22:35.500 --> 00:22:38.080
we win the whole central battle!

00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:49.660
My path--

00:22:49.660 --> 00:22:50.700
It's clear!

00:23:06.540 --> 00:23:09.370
A sword-strike to the thigh while on horseback?

00:23:09.370 --> 00:23:10.750
That's lethal.

00:23:12.830 --> 00:23:14.250
Shit...

00:23:29.580 --> 00:23:38.870
<i>Who will I be when we</i>
<i>meet after all these days?</i>

00:23:38.870 --> 00:23:49.950
<i>Though I hesitate, even fumble,</i>
<i>I keep an eye on my someday dream</i>

00:23:49.950 --> 00:23:59.700
<i>Gathering feathers won't let me fly</i>

00:23:59.700 --> 00:24:04.700
<i>But whenever I find what isn't here</i>

00:24:04.700 --> 00:24:10.330
<i>You're always where I'm searching</i>

00:24:10.330 --> 00:24:15.580
<i>I'll piece together these tattered wishes</i>

00:24:15.580 --> 00:24:20.790
<i>And come tell them to you</i>

00:24:20.790 --> 00:24:25.950
<i>Alone, I picture my burning feelings</i>

00:24:25.950 --> 00:24:31.080
<i>As they overflow</i>

00:24:31.080 --> 00:24:36.330
<i>I'll piece together these tattered wishes</i>

00:24:36.330 --> 00:24:40.580
<i>And come tell them to you</i>

00:24:40.580 --> 00:24:43.830
<i>So we'll make it in time</i>

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:58.010
"Next Episode Preview"

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:07.020
"In a Heartbeat"
